bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    deprecated_removed_spec_closure_capture_mutation_not_visible_2026_11_10, 0, "2026-11-10 filed from code_quality_specs_import_modules_that_do_not_exist_2026-08-04 triage; seed interpreter run: 13 executed, 11 passed, 2 failed."
    deprecated_removed_spec_closure_capture_mutation_not_visible_2026_11_10, 1, "2026-11-10 closed-obsolete (premise outdated): owner ruling 2026-09-27 (.claude/rules/language.md Runtime Limitations; src/compiler/10.frontend/core/capture_write_check.spl, seed capture_write_check.rs) makes closures capture enclosing LOCALS by value and read-only; a method mutation (seen.push) on a captured local is a dropped write on the by-value snapshot on every engine, and an assignment is a compile error. The interpreter is correct; the spec used an unsupported pattern. Re-scoped: deprecated_removed_spec.spl cases :176/:199 now accumulate through module-level vars (each_seen_chars/each_seen_ints), 11/13 -> 13/13 on the seed interpreter. Prevention/policy pin: test/01_unit/interpreter/closure_capture_writeback_spec.spl (7/7: each, text_each, plain fn callback, scalar assign, nested, loop via module-level var; captured local array stays a 0-length snapshot). Follow-up candidate: capture_write_check does not flag mutating method calls (push/insert) on a captured local, so that write is silently dropped rather than rejected."
